The FIRST final matrix of this iteration (before the walk local was renamed and before the Cargo.toml comment was corrected), started 03:47 with 2.7 GB free and incremental caches on.
Two commands failed with `linking with cc failed`: the two with the large `ort`-linked test binary. **[INFERENCE] That was the disk**: the same commands linked at 3.5 GB free (the baseline) and at 3.7 GB with incremental caches off (matrix-final.log), the script's summary
keeps no line of `ld`'s message (so `errno=28` was not seen), and the machine had 2.7 GB free with this session's release builds of `render`, `perfcheck` and three scratch examples still in target/release (the matrix script's own clean removes this crate's DEBUG artifacts only).
It was addressed by `cargo clean --release -p bevy_siren` (235 files, 1.6 GiB, this crate's own artifacts) and by running the final matrix with CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 (matrix-final.log). Everything else in this run was green: 9 + 233 + 7 doc, serde 9 + 242, mixer 20 + 248,
doc 7, readme 1, build --examples, clippy, fmt, rustdoc.
